# S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car's "up to one target creature": Bot1 chooses none (Target()), so the Llanowar Elves and both Ornithopters stay and
# nothing is exiled or returned. On turn 3 Crew 1 is paid by tapping the Elves, power 1 (CR 702.122a: exactly the power the cost
# names; the two Ornithopters, power 0 each, cannot pay it: the refusal), the Car becomes a 3/3 artifact creature and its attack, unblocked, takes Bot2 to 17.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter x2
S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car
Island x2
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target()
[Bot1.Main2]
? Exile.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Llanowar Elves; Ornithopter; Ornithopter; S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car.Activate(Ability: Crew)
! Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car.Types = Artifact; Creature
